      "title": "High velocity gradient, short time",
      "description": "Coagulants (alum, ferric salts, PACl) react within seconds, so they must be spread through the whole flow almost instantly. Flash mixers use high energy — velocity gradient G ≈ 300–1000 s⁻¹ — with short detention (≈ 10–60 s). Too little mixing wastes chemical; too long or too intense mixing is not useful at this stage.",
